{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00386",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.36,
      "end_seconds": 6.78,
      "duration_seconds": 5.42,
      "text": "Hi doctor, sorry, the lift was out and I had to take the stairs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.98,
      "end_seconds": 11.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "Yes, do sit. Tell me what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 11.89,
      "end_seconds": 15.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "Hello, doctor, I came in with them, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 16.92,
      "end_seconds": 23.1,
      "duration_seconds": 6.18,
      "text": "Yeah, uh, it's itchy raised red welts. I don't know what's causing it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.19,
      "end_seconds": 26.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "How long have you had it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.68,
      "end_seconds": 32.49,
      "duration_seconds": 5.81,
      "text": "About... well, one week. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.95,
      "end_seconds": 40.23,
      "duration_seconds": 7.28,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.94,
      "end_seconds": 54.64,
      "duration_seconds": 13.7,
      "text": "Antihistamines helps a bit. Mild, I'd say. Honestly, once or twice a day. I told myself I'd wait and see, and here I am. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.29,
      "end_seconds": 60.11,
      "duration_seconds": 4.82,
      "text": "I was just going to say that the main thing is—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 60.21,
      "end_seconds": 65.79,
      "duration_seconds": 5.58,
      "text": "Sorry to cut in, doctor, quick question: shall I bring the trolley in now or later?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.17,
      "end_seconds": 68.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "Later, thanks. Please go on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 69.38,
      "end_seconds": 74.74,
      "duration_seconds": 5.36,
      "text": "Oh, uh, and welts that move around. Had that since Monday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.03,
      "end_seconds": 80.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.77,
      "text": "Have you had itchy raised red welts before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.6,
      "end_seconds": 85.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "I had a similar thing last winter. It went away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 86.93,
      "end_seconds": 88.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "Yes, exactly like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.99,
      "end_seconds": 95.22,
      "duration_seconds": 5.23,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any new medicines, joint pain or throat tightness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.8,
      "end_seconds": 109.43,
      "duration_seconds": 12.63,
      "text": "No, uh, no new medicines, no joint pain, no throat tightness. I did have a burning feeling on the skin at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.32,
      "end_seconds": 111.02,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Any fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.7,
      "end_seconds": 113.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "Not at all, no fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 115.21,
      "end_seconds": 119.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.56,
      "text": "Actually, you know, doctor, I did notice fever. He doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.13,
      "end_seconds": 127.72,
      "duration_seconds": 6.59,
      "text": "Hmm, no, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.69,
      "end_seconds": 135.97,
      "duration_seconds": 7.28,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Right, have you had any trouble breathing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.68,
      "end_seconds": 140.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "No, uh, I haven't had any trouble breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.35,
      "end_seconds": 143.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "Your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.54,
      "end_seconds": 145.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "No, my breathing's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.14,
      "end_seconds": 149.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "Any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.0,
      "end_seconds": 159.01,
      "duration_seconds": 8.01,
      "text": "I'm on Seretide inhaler, twice a day. I, I take tamsulosin, 0.4 milligrams, at night for the prostate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.72,
      "end_seconds": 166.41,
      "duration_seconds": 5.69,
      "text": "It's a... um, I can't remember what it's called. It's a small white one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.87,
      "end_seconds": 169.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.98,
      "end_seconds": 184.31,
      "duration_seconds": 10.33,
      "text": "For the fluid, I believe. My son sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given. Cetirizine, 10 milligrams, at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 185.22,
      "end_seconds": 189.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 5 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.03,
      "end_seconds": 194.05,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "Right, hm. Do you have the latest prescription with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.18,
      "end_seconds": 198.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.69,
      "end_seconds": 202.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "Do you have everything you need to get home alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 203.3,
      "end_seconds": 214.34,
      "duration_seconds": 11.04,
      "text": "Yes, I've got my transport sorted. It's a bit of a trek, but I'm used to the journey by now, and I brought something to read for the wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.83,
      "end_seconds": 216.68,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 217.63,
      "end_seconds": 229.19,
      "duration_seconds": 11.56,
      "text": "Hmm, uh, there was some antibiotic, I was told I was allergic. But I couldn't tell you what it was called or what it did."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.91,
      "end_seconds": 231.21,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "Do you drink alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 232.26,
      "end_seconds": 234.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "I don't drink at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.85,
      "end_seconds": 236.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "Have you had any surgery before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 239.2,
      "end_seconds": 243.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.38,
      "text": "Yes, I had a hernia repair, about five years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.31,
      "end_seconds": 249.94,
      "duration_seconds": 5.63,
      "text": "Moving on to your background, any past medical history? I'll explain everything as we go along."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 251.35,
      "end_seconds": 264.44,
      "duration_seconds": 13.09,
      "text": "Hmm, I have eczema, for five years. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit. I mean, yes, asthma. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite. An enlarged prostate, for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.78,
      "end_seconds": 265.48,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 266.74,
      "end_seconds": 273.41,
      "duration_seconds": 6.67,
      "text": "I, I have heart failure, for about a year. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.33,
      "end_seconds": 275.32,
      "duration_seconds": 0.99,
      "text": "Okay. Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.67,
      "end_seconds": 287.86,
      "duration_seconds": 11.19,
      "text": "Okay, eczema, that's already on your record. Good to know. Yes, I can see the heart failure in your file as well. What about family history, any illnesses that run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 288.4,
      "end_seconds": 290.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "My father had a stroke."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.13,
      "end_seconds": 305.0,
      "duration_seconds": 13.87,
      "text": "Let me explain how I'm thinking about this. When someone has symptoms like these, we first look for the common and treatable causes, and only then for the rarer ones. That's why I'm going step by step rather than ordering everything at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 306.4,
      "end_seconds": 308.21,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 309.02,
      "end_seconds": 315.73,
      "duration_seconds": 6.71,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Saturation 98 percent, temperature 36.5, BP is 120 over 72. Pulse 76."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 316.8,
      "end_seconds": 333.54,
      "duration_seconds": 16.74,
      "text": "Good, thank you. So, based on your history, this looks most like acute urticaria, possibly allergic. The reason I say that is that the way you describe it fits together. I can't rule out a viral trigger yet. A drug reaction is also on my list."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 335.0,
      "end_seconds": 337.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "So, doctor, is this dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 338.19,
      "end_seconds": 351.94,
      "duration_seconds": 13.75,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with acute urticaria, possibly allergic do well once it's treated properly. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had itchy raised red welts for one week, mild, and no throat tightness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 355.33,
      "end_seconds": 357.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Yes, you know, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 358.14,
      "end_seconds": 362.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "Have you been able to keep up with your usual activities?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 363.24,
      "end_seconds": 376.77,
      "duration_seconds": 13.53,
      "text": "Well, uh, for the most part, yes. I just carry on and try not to dwell on things too much, though I won't pretend it hasn't crossed my mind a few times."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 378.16,
      "end_seconds": 386.75,
      "duration_seconds": 8.59,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange an allergy test for recurrent urticaria. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 387.85,
      "end_seconds": 390.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "Alright. When can I do that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 391.51,
      "end_seconds": 401.75,
      "duration_seconds": 10.24,
      "text": "I'm going to order blood tests, for urticaria. I'd like you to take prednisolone, 20 milligrams, once a day, for three days. You take it by mouth. It's for hives."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 402.86,
      "end_seconds": 403.73,
      "duration_seconds": 0.87,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 404.38,
      "end_seconds": 432.67,
      "duration_seconds": 28.29,
      "text": "Write down anything new you ate, took or used before this started, even small things. Try to keep a simple diary of when it happens and what you were doing, and bring it to the next visit. Cut down on salt and fried food for now, it really does make a difference. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 433.51,
      "end_seconds": 434.79,
      "duration_seconds": 1.28,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 435.34,
      "end_seconds": 444.67,
      "duration_seconds": 9.33,
      "text": "If your lips or tongue swell more, or you have trouble breathing, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 445.69,
      "end_seconds": 446.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "Okay, I understand."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 447.51,
      "end_seconds": 449.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "Come back in two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 449.79,
      "end_seconds": 450.49,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0068",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 451.43,
      "end_seconds": 457.68,
      "duration_seconds": 6.25,
      "text": "So, I want to be sure we're on the same page. How would you describe the plan?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0069",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 459.06,
      "end_seconds": 467.69,
      "duration_seconds": 8.63,
      "text": "So, I take the prednisolone, 20 milligrams, once a day and come back in two weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0070",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 469.21,
      "end_seconds": 473.62,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. All right, I'll let you go. Any final questions first?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0071",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 475.01,
      "end_seconds": 477.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "Thank you. I'll see you then."
    }
  ]
}